IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rsc-dates`
IMPORT `rsc-rules`
IMPORT `rsc-seat`

-- Rules of the Supreme Court 1971 (WA) -- cases for the plaintiff's questions (rsc-seat.l4). Every expected value is
-- worked by hand from the deposited text, with the rule, and never copied from the encoding's output. Weekdays from the
-- calendar: 1 March 2026 is a Sunday; Good Friday 2026 is 3 April and Easter Monday 6 April; 25 December 2026 is a
-- Friday; 16 January 2027 is a Saturday. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the plaintiff`

§§ `O. 3 rr. 2-4 -- the last day of a period`

-- Order: day it runs from, days, pleading step, needs the office open.
-- 14 days from Sunday 1 March 2026: day 14 is Sunday 15 March; r. 4 moves it to Monday 16 March only if the office is needed.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 1 3 2026) 14 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 1 3 2026) 14 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the day` 16 3 2026
-- r. 3: a pleading from 10 December 2026: 11-23 December are 13 days; 24 December to 15 January not reckoned; 16 January
-- 2027 (a Saturday) is day 14; with the office needed, Monday 18 January.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) 14 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 16 1 2027
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) 14 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the day` 18 1 2027
-- The same period for a step that is not a pleading: 24 December 2026, a Thursday.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) 14 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 24 12 2026
-- The last day before the break: from 9 December, 10-23 December are 14 days.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 9 12 2026) 14 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 23 12 2026
-- r. 2(2): 3 days from Thursday 2 April 2026: Good Friday, the weekend and Easter Monday not reckoned; 7, 8, 9 April.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 2 4 2026) 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 9 4 2026
-- r. 2(2) for 6 days from Friday 6 March 2026: 9-13 March are 5, the weekend skipped, Monday 16 March is the 6th.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 6 3 2026) 6 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 16 3 2026
-- 7 days is not "less than 7": the weekend counts; Friday 13 March.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 6 3 2026) 7 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the day` 13 3 2026

§§ `O. 3 r. 7 -- a year's delay`

-- Last proceeding 10 March 2026: the year after runs 11 March 2026 to 10 March 2027 (fork F7).
#ASSERT `Must I give notice of intention to proceed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 10 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I give notice of intention to proceed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 11 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I give notice of intention to proceed?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- One month's notice given 1 April 2026: the month is 2 April to 1 May; proceed from 2 May.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day I can proceed after my notice?` (`the day` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `the day` 2 5 2026
-- Given 31 January 2027: the month is 1 to 28 February; proceed from 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day I can proceed after my notice?` (`the day` 31 1 2027) EQUALS `the day` 1 3 2027
-- Given 30 January 2027: the month from 31 January has no 31 February, so it ends on 28 February (fork F3).
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day I can proceed after my notice?` (`the day` 30 1 2027) EQUALS `the day` 1 3 2027

§§ `O. 5 r. 11 -- time to appear`

#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `in Western Australia` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `in Western Australia` 299 FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `in Western Australia` 300 FALSE EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `in Western Australia` 599 FALSE EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `in Western Australia` 600 FALSE EQUALS JUST 21
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `in Western Australia` 2200 FALSE EQUALS JUST 21
-- r. 11(2): the Service and Execution of Process Act 1992 (Cth), outside the sources.
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `elsewhere in Australia` 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `outside Australia` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 42
#ASSERT `How many days must my writ give to appear?` `outside Australia` 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `O. 7 -- the writ's validity`

-- 12 months beginning with the day of issue.
#ASSERT `Until when is my writ valid for service?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 14 3 2027
#ASSERT `Until when is my writ valid for service?` (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 12 2026
-- Issued on 29 February 2028: there is no 29 February 2029; the last day of February (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Until when is my writ valid for service?` (`the day` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `the day` 28 2 2029

-- r. 1(2). Order: issued, served, day I apply, the Court allows a later day. Issued 15 March 2026, expiring 14 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Can the Court extend my writ?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`the day` 14 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court extend my writ?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`the day` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court extend my writ?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) FALSE (`the day` 15 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court extend my writ?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) TRUE (`the day` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 12 months beginning with the day after expiry.
#ASSERT `What is the latest day one extension can reach?` (`the day` 14 3 2027) EQUALS `the day` 14 3 2028
-- From 1 March 2027 to 29 February 2028, a leap year.
#ASSERT `What is the latest day one extension can reach?` (`the day` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `the day` 29 2 2028

-- r. 4. Order: issued, direction day, hearing day, affidavit of service filed, appearance entered, the Court accepts my
-- reason. Issued 15 March 2026: the 6 months after run 16 March to 15 September 2026; a direction "after" that is made
-- from 16 September, and the hearing is at least 7 days after the direction: from 23 September at the earliest.
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 15 9 2026) (`the day` 22 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 15 9 2026) (`the day` 30 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 16 9 2026) (`the day` 22 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 16 9 2026) (`the day` 23 9 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 16 9 2026) (`the day` 23 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 16 9 2026) (`the day` 23 9 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my unserved writ be struck out?` (`the day` 15 3 2026) (`the day` 16 9 2026) (`the day` 23 9 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `O. 9 r. 1(4) -- indorsing service`

-- 3 days, closed days not reckoned (O. 3 r. 2(2)).
#ASSERT `By when must service be indorsed on the writ?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 5 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must service be indorsed on the writ?` (`the day` 6 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 11 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must service be indorsed on the writ?` (`the day` 2 4 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 4 2026
-- Served Wednesday 23 December 2026: 24 December (1), Christmas Day and the weekend skipped, 28 (2), 29 (3). 28 December
-- 2026 is the Boxing Day holiday, which is not computed (fork F2): the true last day is probably 30 December.
#ASSERT `By when must service be indorsed on the writ?` (`the day` 23 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 29 12 2026

§§ `O. 5 r. 11(4), O. 3 -- the last day to appear`

#ASSERT `What is the last day for the defendant to appear?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 EQUALS `the day` 12 3 2026
-- Day 10 is Saturday 14 March: r. 4 moves it to Monday 16 March.
#ASSERT `What is the last day for the defendant to appear?` (`the day` 4 3 2026) 10 EQUALS `the day` 16 3 2026
-- Day 11 is Good Friday 3 April 2026: moves past the weekend and Easter Monday to Tuesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `What is the last day for the defendant to appear?` (`the day` 23 3 2026) 11 EQUALS `the day` 7 4 2026
-- Not a pleading, so the Christmas period counts; day 10 is Christmas Day, moved to Monday 28 December (fork F2).
#ASSERT `What is the last day for the defendant to appear?` (`the day` 15 12 2026) 10 EQUALS `the day` 28 12 2026

§§ `O. 13 -- default judgment`

-- Order: kind, served, days to appear, day I would enter it, appeared, solicitor accepted, indorsed in 3 days, affidavit.
-- Served 2 March 2026 with 10 days: the time to appear ends 12 March.
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment, with damages to be assessed by a master`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 12 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none yet: the time to appear has not run out`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none: the defendant has appeared`
-- O. 13 r. 1(3)(a) with O. 9 r. 1(4): personal service needs both the indorsement within 3 days and the affidavit.
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `none yet: service must first be proved`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `none yet: service must first be proved`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `judgment, with damages to be assessed by a master`
-- Each kind of claim, rr. 2-9.
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `a debt or other liquidated demand only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment for the sum claimed and costs`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `detention of goods only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment for the goods or their value, or for their value, to be assessed`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `possession of land only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment for possession and costs, on filing the certificate`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `a mortgage action` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment for the relief and costs, after the mortgage steps`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `two or more of those kinds only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment on each claim as if it were the only one`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `any other claim` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `apply to the Court on motion for judgment`
-- Served 4 March with 10 days: day 10 is a Saturday, so the time runs to Monday 16 March; 16 March is too early.
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 4 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 16 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none yet: the time to appear has not run out`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 4 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 17 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment, with damages to be assessed by a master`
-- O. 10 Division 4: served through foreign officials, no O. 9 r. 1(4) indorsement; the certificate is the affidavit.
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `judgment, with damages to be assessed by a master`
#ASSERT `What default judgment can I enter?` `unliquidated damages only` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 13 3 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `none yet: service must first be proved`

§§ `O. 20 r. 1 -- my statement of claim`

-- Order: day of appearance, indorsed on the writ, the Court gave leave. 14 days from Monday 2 March 2026: Monday 16 March.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my statement of claim?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the day` 16 3 2026)
-- A pleading: from 10 December 2026, to Saturday 16 January 2027 (no r. 4 extension for my own step, fork F5).
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my statement of claim?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the day` 16 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my statement of claim?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my statement of claim?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Order: day of appearance, day served.
#ASSERT `Did I serve my statement of claim in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 16 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I serve my statement of claim in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 17 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I serve my statement of claim in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- Served with the writ, before the appearance.
#ASSERT `Did I serve my statement of claim in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 20 2 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I serve my statement of claim in time?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) (`the day` 16 1 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I serve my statement of claim in time?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) (`the day` 18 1 2027) EQUALS FALSE

§§ `O. 20 r. 4 -- the defence`

-- Order: writ served, days to appear, statement of claim served, summary judgment summons first.
-- Writ and statement of claim served 2 March 2026, 10 days: time to appear ends 12 March; 14 days on, 26 March.
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant serve a defence?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 2 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the day` 26 3 2026)
-- Statement of claim served later, 20 March: 14 days on is Good Friday 3 April; r. 4 moves it to Tuesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant serve a defence?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 20 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the day` 7 4 2026)
-- Writ served 1 December 2026: appear by Friday 11 December; 12-23 December are 12 days, then 16 and 17 January 2027;
-- Sunday 17 January moves to Monday 18 January.
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant serve a defence?` (`the day` 1 12 2026) 10 (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`the day` 18 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must the defendant serve a defence?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 10 (`the day` 2 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `O. 20 rr. 5(4), 20 -- reply and close of pleadings`

#ASSERT `By when must I serve my reply?` (`the day` 26 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 4 2026
-- Defence served 20 December 2026: 21-23 December are 3 days; 16-26 January 2027 the other 11.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my reply?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 26 1 2027
#ASSERT `When do the pleadings close?` (`the day` 9 4 2026) EQUALS `the day` 23 4 2026
-- Not a time for an act: the Christmas period counts (fork F6).
#ASSERT `When do the pleadings close?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 3 1 2027

§§ `O. 14 r. 1 -- summary judgment`

#ASSERT `By when can I apply for summary judgment without leave?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 23 3 2026
-- Day 21 is Good Friday 3 April 2026; my own step, not extended (fork F5).
#ASSERT `By when can I apply for summary judgment without leave?` (`the day` 13 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 3 4 2026

§§ `O. 24A -- offers of compromise`

-- r. 3(4): 3 days, closed days not reckoned.
#ASSERT `By when must I acknowledge the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 5 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I acknowledge the offer?` (`the day` 2 4 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 4 2026
#ASSERT `Did I acknowledge the offer in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 5 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I acknowledge the offer in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 6 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I acknowledge the offer in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I acknowledge the offer in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I acknowledge the offer in time?` (`the day` 2 4 2026) (`the day` 9 4 2026) EQUALS TRUE

-- r. 3(3), (5), (8). Order: offer made, days open (0 none), day I accept, judge has begun. 28 days from 2 March 2026: 30 March.
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 (`the day` 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 (`the day` 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A stated 14 days is below the 28-day floor and is read as 28 (fork F8).
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 14 (`the day` 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 42 days: to 13 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 42 (`the day` 13 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 42 (`the day` 14 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 (`the day` 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 (`the day` 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- r. 4. Order: accepted, days to pay (0 none), paid, day paid, today. Accepted 2 March 2026: 28 days to 30 March.
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the day` 30 3 2026) (`the day` 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the day` 10 3 2026) (`the day` 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The offer gave 60 days: paid on day 49.
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 60 TRUE (`the day` 20 4 2026) (`the day` 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A payment dated after today is not yet made.
#ASSERT `Was the accepted offer paid in time?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) 0 TRUE (`the day` 20 3 2026) (`the day` 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- r. 5. Order: accepted, how paid, day paid, day I withdraw, the Court gives leave. Accepted 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `not paid` (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `not paid` (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `not paid` (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `paid into Court` (`the day` 30 3 2026) (`the day` 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `paid into Court` (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paid to me in time, not into Court: the rule does not address it (finding 1, fork F9).
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `paid to me (not into Court)` (`the day` 20 3 2026) (`the day` 1 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) `paid to me (not into Court)` (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- r. 10. Order: who, sum offered, judgment, interest after the offer, offer on or after the first day of trial, offeror
-- willing and able, not accepting unreasonable, justice requires otherwise, the Court orders otherwise.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 100000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs throughout, on the ordinary basis`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 99999 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no costs consequence from the offer under r. 10`
-- r. 10(7): 6,000 of the 105,000 is interest after the offer: 99,000 counts, short of the offer.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 105000 6000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no costs consequence from the offer under r. 10`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 105000 5000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs throughout, on the ordinary basis`
-- r. 10(5A).
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 150000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs to the offer on the ordinary basis, and from the day of the offer on the indemnity basis`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 150000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs throughout, on the ordinary basis`
-- r. 10(5): a judgment equal to the defendant's offer is "not more favourable".
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 80000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs up to and including the day of the offer; the defendant's costs after it`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 80001 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no costs consequence from the offer under r. 10`
-- r. 10(5) needs "the plaintiff obtains judgment": a claim lost (judgment 0) is not caught, so r. 10 gives nothing.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no costs consequence from the offer under r. 10`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 0 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no costs consequence from the offer under r. 10`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 90000 10000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs up to and including the day of the offer; the defendant's costs after it`
-- r. 10(6), (7A).
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 50000 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs up to 11 a.m. the day after the offer; the defendant's costs after that`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 50000 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs up to 11 a.m. the day after the offer; the defendant's costs after that on the indemnity basis`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 50000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my costs up to and including the day of the offer; the defendant's costs after it on the indemnity basis`
-- r. 10(3): not willing and able: subrules (4) and (5) do not apply.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `the defendant did` 80000 50000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no costs consequence from the offer under r. 10`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the offer?` `I did` 100000 150000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- rr. 8, 9. Order: defendant failed to comply, special cause, jointly liable defendants, offer covers all of them.
#ASSERT `Can I have the defence struck out for breach of the accepted offer?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I have the defence struck out for breach of the accepted offer?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I have the defence struck out for breach of the accepted offer?` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I have the defence struck out for breach of the accepted offer?` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I have the defence struck out for breach of the accepted offer?` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `O. 23 -- discontinuance`

-- Order: received the defence, taken another step since.
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I discontinue without leave?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the defendant's costs if I discontinue?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I pay the defendant's costs if I discontinue?` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my new action be stayed until I pay the old costs?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my new action be stayed until I pay the old costs?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my new action be stayed until I pay the old costs?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `O. 25 -- security for costs`

#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I ordinarily live outside Western Australia` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I am about to leave Western Australia` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I am immune from execution here` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I am an undischarged bankrupt or have suspended payment of my debts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I am a company in liquidation, official management or receivership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I am suing as a relator for a public right, trust or charity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I have not paid costs ordered in an earlier case on the same matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I have vexatiously sued before` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `I am suing the sheriff about an execution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `only that I am poor or could not pay the costs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- r. 1 is general; r. 2 does not limit it.
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to give security for costs?` `some other reason` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Order: ordered, given, the Court ordered no stay.
#ASSERT `Is my action stayed until I give security?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my action stayed until I give security?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my action stayed until I give security?` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my action stayed until I give security?` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `O. 28 r. 1 -- medical examination`

-- Order: condition material, notice served, their doctor at their cost, the Court ordered I need not attend.
#ASSERT `Must I attend the defendant's medical examination?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I attend the defendant's medical examination?` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I attend the defendant's medical examination?` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I attend the defendant's medical examination?` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I attend the defendant's medical examination?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the defendant pay my examination expenses?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the defendant pay my examination expenses?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Order: copy served, a week has passed, I say it is incomplete.
#ASSERT `Can I get an order for the medical report?` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I get an order for the medical report?` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get an order for the medical report?` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I get an order for the medical report?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get an order for the medical report?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `O. 70 -- persons under disability`

-- Order: under 18, represented person, declared incapable, a judge permitted me to sue alone.
#ASSERT `Must I sue by a next friend?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I sue by a next friend?` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I sue by a next friend?` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- r. 2(4) permits an infant only: a child who is also a represented person still needs a next friend.
#ASSERT `Must I sue by a next friend?` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I sue by a next friend?` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I sue by a next friend?` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Order: under 18, represented, declared incapable, proceedings begun, an appeal, the Court approved it.
#ASSERT `Is my settlement valid without the Court's approval?` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my settlement valid without the Court's approval?` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my settlement valid without the Court's approval?` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my settlement valid without the Court's approval?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my settlement valid without the Court's approval?` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my settlement valid without the Court's approval?` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Order: under 18, represented, declared incapable, the Court ordered otherwise.
#ASSERT `Where will the money recovered for me be paid?` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to the Public Trustee, to invest for me`
#ASSERT `Where will the money recovered for me be paid?` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as the Court orders`
#ASSERT `Where will the money recovered for me be paid?` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the disability rule does not apply`

§§ `O. 4A Division 5 -- inactive cases`

-- r. 24: last step 10 March 2026; 12 months to 10 March 2027; inactive from 11 March 2027.
#ASSERT `From when is my case taken to be inactive?` (`the day` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 11 3 2027
-- 29 February 2028: the 12 months run 1 March 2028 to 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `From when is my case taken to be inactive?` (`the day` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `the day` 1 3 2029
#ASSERT `From when is my case taken to be inactive?` (`the day` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `the day` 1 9 2027

-- r. 28. Order: notice day, taken off, day taken off, step since, day of first step since, today.
-- Notice 1 April 2027: 6 months run 2 April to 1 October 2027.
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 1 10 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 2 10 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Taken off on the last day, 1 October 2027: r. 28(2), 6 months from 2 October 2027 to 1 April 2028.
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the day` 1 10 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 2 10 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the day` 1 10 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 1 4 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the day` 1 10 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 2 4 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the day` 1 10 2027) TRUE (`the day` 1 4 2028) (`the day` 3 4 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the day` 1 10 2027) TRUE (`the day` 2 4 2028) (`the day` 3 4 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Taken off only after the 6 months on the list had run: already dismissed under r. 28(1).
#ASSERT `Has my case been dismissed for inactivity?` (`the day` 1 4 2027) TRUE (`the day` 5 10 2027) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2000) (`the day` 10 10 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `Regulative rules`

-- O. 20 r. 1: 14 days, service on day 14.
#TRACE `O. 20 r. 1 -- my duty to serve the statement of claim` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the plaintiff` DOES `serve the statement of claim` AT 14

-- O. 24A r. 3(4): served Monday 2 March 2026, 3 days to Thursday 5 March; acknowledged on day 3.
#TRACE `O. 24A r. 3(4) -- my duty to acknowledge the offer` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the plaintiff` DOES `acknowledge receipt of the offer` AT 3

-- O. 24A r. 4: 28 days; paid on day 28.
#TRACE `O. 24A r. 4 -- the defendant's duty to pay` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the defendant` DOES `pay the sum offered` AT 28
